These are the fundamental changes we are going to implement:

1. In MCH_WIP we have two types of Production Orders.,
	1. ORDER_STATUS is "Active". These are Production orders for which the foundry materials are available in shop floor, assigned to those respective Production Orders for Machining Process to start. These orders should be planned as usual (check the CDD, batch the orders according to batching logic and assign to machines based on the operation and priority.) No external logic constraint is required.
	2. ORDER_STATUS is "Planned". These are Production Orders for which the foundry materials are C.N.A (Currently Not Available) in the shop floor, but materials assigned for those respective production orders but the date at which the foundry materials will arrive on the shop floor will be on their respective PRODUCTION_START_DATE_AND_TIME column of MCH_WIP. In this case the Engine1 has to plan the production to start for that order at PRODUCTION_START_DATE_AND_TIME + 1 day or near that day (consider that dates (PRODUCTION_START_DATE_AND_TIME + 1 day) first shift also) and to be delivered before its CDD. 
Always EVERY PRODUCTION ORDER SHOULD BE TRIED TO DELIVER ON OR BEFORE ITS CDD.

2. BATCHING Information:
	I will explain the Batching Information here, there will be clear cut explanation on BATCHING LOGIC and accurate explanation with more specfic Example down below, but try to understand from this explanation and correlate it with the logic.
		1. Now the Whole concept of adding SETUP_TIME before every First Piece is lost and rather we add a Concept of Fixture and Locator. See, every SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN will have Locator attached to a Fixture. See every PARTICULAR SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN will have Fixed Fixture and Locator and every similar SIZE~CLASS will have Fixture same but only the Locator change.
		2. When the Fixture is changed, both the FIXTURE_CHANGE_TIME (Time taken to change the Fixture) and LOCATOR_CHANGE_TIME (Time taken to change the Locator) from the MCH_ITEMWISE_FIXTURE_LOCATOR table, is added before the first piece of that batch.
		3. When only the Locator is changed, the LOCATOR_CHANGE_TIME from the MCH_ITEMWISE_FIXTURE_LOCATOR table, is added.
		4. Apart from this LOAD_UNLOAD_TIME is added for every piece in that batch so LOAD_UNLOAD_TIME should be multiplied with total quantity of that Batch which Engine1 has grouped.
		5. Same SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN and Same operation should not be ideally carried out in different machine at same time or instance ., For Example if an 10~150~Carbon steel~DF order is planned for Op10 today., I want the algorithm to combine all the orders of same 10~150~Carbon steel~DF on operation 10 with same Fixture and Locator (or) same Fixture but different Locator to be grouped together on the same day at maximum cases.
		6. A fixed SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN will have fixed FIXTURE and LOCATOR in MCH_ITEMWISE_FIXTURE_LOCATOR., in cases where orders of batch may consist of both Priority orders (CDD is not null) and Safety Stock order (where CDD is null) and when these batches go through higher time consuming Task like VB03 (Weld overlay), Stemboring, Cone Finish and StemBore + Cone Finish (VB04, VB05, VB06), It is usually better to go with batch without Safety stock. In those case u might consider safety stock as last priority., but I still need your help on how to handle this situation. 
		   6.1. But An important thing is in MCH_FIXTURE_LOCATOR table you will give you information on how many fixture (DEVICE_NAME = (Fixture ID) and DEVICE_TYPE = "F") are available on that particular Fixture ID in our shop floor material stock and simililarly No of Locators (DEVICE_NAME = (Locator ID) and DEVICE_TYPE = "L") of that particular Locator ID in our shop floor material stock. We HAVE already added two new columns in MCH_SCHEDULE_OUTPUT (Engine1 result) in such a way that every time we assign a production order of an operation to a Machine we have to record the Fixture ID and Locator ID from DEVICE_NAME of MCH_FIXTURE_LOCATOR and record it in the two new columns created in MCH_SCHEDULE_OUTPUT, this is done because there are only a fixed no of Fixtures and Locators., and the batching should take that into consideration.
		7. In MCH_SCHEDULE_OUTPUT I want you to help add a column called "REMARK" at the end. See the MCH_SCHEDULE_OUTPUT will have all records of Production Orders that are schedulable (alloted into batches and assigned machine, fixture, locator etc., ) from MCP_WIP. but for some orders there will be no allocation of Machine/Fixture and locator. So update the reason in this remark field that should be human readable / understandable.
		
3. Fixture Logic
    See certain group of SIZE's (valves) will have same fixture, you can even verify this with the data in MCH_ITEMWISE_FIXTURE_LOCATOR. I have mentioned those groups below:
	3.1. 3" - 6" (" - Inch)
	3.2. 8" - 14"
	3.3. 16" - 24"
	3.4. 26" - 36"
	3.5. 40" - 48"
	But there are a few exceptions
	3.6. If the DESIGN = "DFL" the fixture might change with respect to fixtures of other, same or similar SIZE~CLASS and different DESIGN's (DFS, LUG, WAF)
	3.7. If the CLASS = "600" the fixture might change with respect to fixtures of other, same or similar SIZE (within those groupes).
	
4. TIMING LOGIC:
	4.1. Whenever a Fixture is changed time calculation should be: FIXTURE_CHANGE_TIME + LOCATOR_CHANGE_TIME + LOAD_UNLOAD_TIME * QTY (per piece LOAD_UNLOAD_TIME)
	4.2. Whenever a Locator is changed time calculation should be: LOCATOR_CHANGE_TIME + LOAD_UNLOAD_TIME * QTY

5. BATCHING LOGIC: 
The Batching should always be done to reduce the overall Production Time of the machines of shop floor (By combining similar type Production Orders together) and maximizing Machine Utilization to produce better results
	5.1. All the Production Orders which have same Fixtures and are to be assigned to a specfic machine for a specific operation should be combined to create a batch first, to reduce Fixture change time. Within that Batch combine all same SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN, then go to similar SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN with same fixture and Locator, then group it with orders where only LOCATOR is changed (here LOCATOR_CHANGE_TIME is added).
	5.2. In that batch all the Production Orders with same SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN (exact same) should be combined together at first then combine similar SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN with same FIXTURE and LOCATOR type, then batch it with same FIXTURE but Different LOCATOR, and then finally go to different batch with different fixture and locator setting. When going to next batch always focus on CDD priority.
	5.3. First identify the priority by CDD., then start batching that exact same SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN (within same machine and same task), then similar SIZE~CLASS~MOC~DESIGN with SAME FIXTURE AND LOCATOR for that machine and task, then go with same fixture but just different Locator and then go with a different batch that follows the same procedure.

6. Planning Production Continously :
	1. DO NOT PLAN SHIFT WISE., the plan should always be continuous. If a batch with a specific operation is completed in a Machine., that Machine should not be left ideal for not more than 20 mins., that is after completion of a Batch activity and 20 mins of cooling period that machine should be given the next task at 21st minute ( > or = 20 mins ). It doesn't matter if the 21st minute falls on same shift (or) the next shift (or) next available shift on a different day. Production should always be not ideal.
	2. DO NOT have Capacity Restrictions on any Machine. All the Machines can load Infinte Capacity and Time. Production orders of specific Operation is alloted to Machine only based on Batch Priority, Machine Availability, Fixture and Locator availability and Maximum Machine Utilization.
	3. See always consider all the Machine available into consideration while planning., do not plan only on a few machines and keep some machine ideal. If Machine is breakdown or unavailable then that information will be available on MCH_MACHINE_AVAILABILITY_BY_DATE, with which you can plan accordingly, but if there is no data regarding a machine then always consider that machine is available for all AVAILABLE_MINS (in MCH_MACHINE_AVAILABILITY, for all shifts all day and include it in plan.
	
